1
00:00:43,875 --> 00:00:44,900
<i>Huh?</i>

2
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:46,932
<i>My alumna, Shin Bi Gyeong?</i>

3
00:00:46,932 --> 00:00:49,195
Hello, it's 2013.

4
00:00:49,195 --> 00:00:51,058
<i>2013?</i>

5
00:00:51,058 --> 00:00:55,280
<i>Did the rain trigger another time leap?</i>

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:57,199
<i>Huh? Ye Rang...</i>

7
00:00:57,199 --> 00:00:58,395
<i>and Jun Mo!</i>

8
00:00:58,395 --> 00:01:00,118
Bottoms up.

9
00:01:00,118 --> 00:01:03,106
- Let's hand it over to reporter Yoon Ha Na.
<i>- Yoon Ha Na?</i>

10
00:01:03,106 --> 00:01:05,937
<i>- Yoon Ha Na?</i>
- Reporter Yoon Ha Na...

11
00:01:05,937 --> 00:01:07,605
Did you just call me...

12
00:01:07,605 --> 00:01:10,005
Yoon Ha Na?

13
00:01:11,038 --> 00:01:13,204
It's me!

14
00:01:13,204 --> 00:01:15,227
It's Yoon Ha Na!

15
00:01:18,679 --> 00:01:20,469
But why 2013?

16
00:01:20,469 --> 00:01:23,409
Why not 2026? Why is it 2013?

17
00:01:23,409 --> 00:01:24,893
What's wrong, Ha Na?

18
00:01:24,893 --> 00:01:26,296
You alright, Ha Na?

19
00:01:26,296 --> 00:01:28,389
I'd be 21 in 2013...

20
00:01:28,389 --> 00:01:30,167
So, if he's 21...

21
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:32,680
Woo Jae must be serving in the army.

22
00:01:35,830 --> 00:01:37,514
- Hey, Yoon Ha Na!
- Yoon Ha Na!

23
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:39,214
Hey, where are you going?

24
00:01:40,935 --> 00:01:43,106
She must be drunk.

25
00:01:43,106 --> 00:01:45,807
Oh, right. Jun Mo.

26
00:01:45,807 --> 00:01:50,110
When are the audition results
for the female lead coming out?

27
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,801
It's still under evaluation by the professor.

28
00:01:51,801 --> 00:01:52,963
But soon, I think.

29
00:01:52,963 --> 00:01:54,186
Oh, I see.

30
00:01:54,186 --> 00:01:56,991
Hey, it's not even that promising a script.

31
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:58,385
What's with the delay, huh?

32
00:01:58,385 --> 00:02:02,031
He's a, uh, he's an odd one, you hear?

33
00:02:03,793 --> 00:02:05,696
Why is this happening?

34
00:02:05,696 --> 00:02:08,018
What went wrong?

35
00:02:08,018 --> 00:02:11,394
[Beast]
Why won't he answer?

36
00:02:13,665 --> 00:02:15,312
Oh, my purse!

37
00:02:15,312 --> 00:02:16,403
Thief!

38
00:02:16,403 --> 00:02:19,155
- Move!
- It's a thief! A thief!

39
00:02:21,404 --> 00:02:22,560
Move!

40
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:24,960
- He's a thief!
- Out of the way!

41
00:02:26,121 --> 00:02:28,197
You're not going anywhere!

42
00:02:29,291 --> 00:02:31,033
Piss off!

43
00:02:36,407 --> 00:02:37,947
Let go!

44
00:02:40,393 --> 00:02:41,417
Are you alright?

45
00:02:41,417 --> 00:02:43,312
Woo Jae!

46
00:02:47,896 --> 00:02:50,557
- Let go!
- Stay down, you scum!

47
00:02:50,557 --> 00:02:52,341
Are you hurt?

48
00:03:04,239 --> 00:03:06,469
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

49
00:03:06,469 --> 00:03:08,416
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

50
00:03:08,416 --> 00:03:10,816
- A bottle of soju, please.
- A soju, coming right up!

51
00:03:34,476 --> 00:03:35,805
[10:46 PM]
[2013/05/31 Friday]

52
00:03:41,709 --> 00:03:43,164
[Yoon's Raw Fish Restaurant]

53
00:03:46,535 --> 00:03:48,651
What are you delaying for?
We're busy enough as is!

54
00:03:48,651 --> 00:03:51,106
- Mom!
- Seriously!

55
00:03:51,106 --> 00:03:52,481
Hi, Mom...

56
00:03:53,925 --> 00:03:56,663
- What am I doing here?
- Oh, my!

57
00:03:56,663 --> 00:03:58,221
You still haven't prepared these?

58
00:03:58,221 --> 00:03:59,757
Really, what have you been doing?

59
00:03:59,757 --> 00:04:00,993
What?

60
00:04:01,601 --> 00:04:03,123
How would I even do this?

61
00:04:03,123 --> 00:04:04,256
I've never done this before!

62
00:04:04,256 --> 00:04:07,319
What are you on about?

63
00:04:07,319 --> 00:04:10,483
You've been hacking off
fish heads all day, see that pile?

64
00:04:10,483 --> 00:04:13,478
Come up with a better excuse next time.

65
00:04:13,478 --> 00:04:14,988
Hey, you. Go to Seoul.

66
00:04:14,988 --> 00:04:17,431
I'm taking an hour's worth of wages
off of today's shift.

67
00:04:20,827 --> 00:04:22,319
Shift?

68
00:04:22,319 --> 00:04:23,932
What shift?

69
00:04:26,748 --> 00:04:28,515
Am I working part-time here?

70
00:04:29,105 --> 00:04:30,988
You said, once you graduate culinary school,

71
00:04:30,988 --> 00:04:34,329
you'll open a restaurant in Gangnam
and make us proud.

72
00:04:34,329 --> 00:04:38,093
Proud, my butt. I'm more concerned
about you blowing your tuition.

73
00:04:39,452 --> 00:04:41,249
Restaurant?

74
00:04:41,956 --> 00:04:43,425
Bodyguard?

75
00:04:43,425 --> 00:04:45,073
Yeah.

76
00:04:53,747 --> 00:04:55,128
[Beast]

77
00:04:56,057 --> 00:04:57,797
One moment.

78
00:04:57,797 --> 00:04:59,303
Okay.

79
00:05:02,642 --> 00:05:04,428
What took you so long?

80
00:05:04,428 --> 00:05:05,874
Yoon Ha Ru, where are you right now?

81
00:05:05,874 --> 00:05:07,742
Working part-time at our parents' restaurant.

82
00:05:07,742 --> 00:05:09,504
I'm not a judo player.

83
00:05:09,504 --> 00:05:12,028
<i>I gave up... on judo.</i>

84
00:05:12,028 --> 00:05:13,273
What?

85
00:05:14,266 --> 00:05:15,708
Where are you?

86
00:05:15,708 --> 00:05:17,133
I'm near the campus.

87
00:05:17,133 --> 00:05:19,218
And I'm me, Yoon Ha Na. I'm in my body.

88
00:05:19,218 --> 00:05:20,465
Well, me too.

89
00:05:20,465 --> 00:05:22,693
I'm Yoon Ha Ru, myself.

90
00:05:22,693 --> 00:05:24,176
It's 2013...

91
00:05:24,176 --> 00:05:27,377
I'm in the class of 2012 at Yongwon University,
a sophomore in film. You?

92
00:05:27,377 --> 00:05:29,764
I'm studying culinary arts at Yongwon.

93
00:05:29,764 --> 00:05:32,834
I'm a freshman. Class of 2013.

94
00:05:33,467 --> 00:05:34,957
Woo Jae isn't a national player, either.

95
00:05:34,957 --> 00:05:36,984
Security services, Yongwon, class of 2012...

96
00:05:36,984 --> 00:05:38,970
Nothing's going as we expected.

97
00:05:38,970 --> 00:05:40,335
Yeah, no joke.

98
00:05:40,335 --> 00:05:42,776
<i>Let's talk in person.</i>

99
00:05:42,776 --> 00:05:46,549
Yeah, I'll take the first train
leaving tomorrow.

100
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:00,477
Are you done?

101
00:06:00,477 --> 00:06:03,332
Yeah, Ha Ru seems busy.

102
00:06:03,332 --> 00:06:04,483
Of course.

103
00:06:04,483 --> 00:06:06,741
There are always lots of customers
at this hour.

104
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:08,866
- Let's go.
- Huh?

105
00:06:09,745 --> 00:06:11,122
Okay...

106
00:06:39,586 --> 00:06:41,124
[2012 National Judo Tournament]

107
00:06:59,188 --> 00:07:01,306
Hey, kiddo.

108
00:07:02,585 --> 00:07:04,686
Kiddo.

109
00:07:04,686 --> 00:07:06,411
Dad?

110
00:07:06,411 --> 00:07:08,777
You trouble-making, naughty,
mischievous little bastard...

111
00:07:08,777 --> 00:07:11,636
Can't even bother to stand up
at your father's grand arrival?

112
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:13,991
Are you drunk?

113
00:07:13,991 --> 00:07:16,953
No, I'm not... Hey! Get up!

114
00:07:16,953 --> 00:07:19,189
I... Okay.

115
00:07:20,218 --> 00:07:22,125
Attention.

116
00:07:22,125 --> 00:07:24,687
Don't you dare use your judo skills on me.

117
00:07:24,687 --> 00:07:26,987
Stay still. Arms at your side...

118
00:07:27,630 --> 00:07:30,727
Aw, my cutie-pie little sonny boy...

119
00:07:32,135 --> 00:07:34,873
What's wrong with you?

120
00:07:40,743 --> 00:07:42,602
Oh, you...

121
00:07:43,438 --> 00:07:45,258
My boy.

122
00:07:50,144 --> 00:07:52,614
How's school going?

123
00:07:52,614 --> 00:07:54,991
How's your cooking?

124
00:07:54,991 --> 00:07:58,694
You must be standing up all day in the kitchen.

125
00:07:58,694 --> 00:08:00,509
Are your legs alright?

126
00:08:05,835 --> 00:08:08,654
Yeah, it's fine, I think.

127
00:08:10,502 --> 00:08:12,963
Cooking's not easy, you know...

128
00:08:12,963 --> 00:08:17,915
Hey, I heard they run kitchens like the army.
They've got nags and bullies, right?

129
00:08:17,915 --> 00:08:19,290
I say...

130
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:22,058
if anyone tries to bully you,
let me know right away.

131
00:08:22,058 --> 00:08:24,562
I'll go there and take care of stuff!

132
00:08:24,562 --> 00:08:27,107
I'm not a kid anymore!

133
00:08:27,107 --> 00:08:29,734
Dad, this is Yoon Ha Ru we're talking about.

134
00:08:29,734 --> 00:08:31,361
Bullying?

135
00:08:31,361 --> 00:08:32,779
I doubt I'd care.

136
00:08:32,779 --> 00:08:35,179
I mean, I won't!

137
00:08:35,779 --> 00:08:37,646
Stop worrying.

138
00:08:46,251 --> 00:08:48,253
Deary me.

139
00:08:48,253 --> 00:08:51,997
I don't recall you growing up so fast.

140
00:08:53,633 --> 00:08:55,718
I remember when you used to waddle...

141
00:08:55,718 --> 00:08:59,347
and refuse to leave my side
like it was yesterday.

142
00:08:59,347 --> 00:09:02,767
And now you're saying
you'll become a great cook,

143
00:09:02,767 --> 00:09:05,167
and make us proud.

144
00:09:07,188 --> 00:09:10,233
Not a cook, a chef.

145
00:09:10,233 --> 00:09:12,050
Yeah, yeah.

146
00:09:12,050 --> 00:09:14,907
- Cook.
- No, a chef...

147
00:09:17,824 --> 00:09:19,426
Sure.

148
00:09:21,494 --> 00:09:23,583
- Dad.
- Yeah?

149
00:09:25,586 --> 00:09:29,916
Remember why I quit judo?

150
00:09:32,043 --> 00:09:34,498
Of course I do.

151
00:09:34,498 --> 00:09:37,042
How would I forget?

152
00:09:38,249 --> 00:09:41,669
They said the surgery went great.

153
00:09:41,669 --> 00:09:45,158
So we all thought you'd make a full recovery
and jump straight back into judo...

154
00:09:49,272 --> 00:09:50,887
<i>Oh, boy.</i>

155
00:09:56,605 --> 00:10:01,850
<i>If he keeps competing,
he might lose the ability to walk.</i>

156
00:10:01,850 --> 00:10:05,068
<i>I wouldn't recommend that he keep playing judo.</i>

157
00:10:05,068 --> 00:10:06,698
<i>Dad...</i>

158
00:10:08,988 --> 00:10:10,794
<i>My boy...</i>

159
00:10:11,699 --> 00:10:13,173
<i>It's okay.</i>

160
00:10:18,884 --> 00:10:21,192
<i>Cry as much as you want, my boy.</i>

161
00:10:25,121 --> 00:10:27,547
You know, I really...

162
00:10:27,547 --> 00:10:30,760
I'm a man of simple wishes.

163
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,845
I just want you two...

164
00:10:32,845 --> 00:10:36,465
Ha Ru and Ha Na...

165
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:41,271
to stay healthy, like right now.

166
00:10:41,271 --> 00:10:44,176
All would be well if you two are well.

167
00:10:44,892 --> 00:10:47,386
I, Yoon Chang Sik...

168
00:10:47,386 --> 00:10:49,786
want nothing else in life.

169
00:10:53,390 --> 00:10:55,570
Hey, come on. Pour me a shot.

170
00:10:55,570 --> 00:10:57,118
Okay.

171
00:11:06,941 --> 00:11:08,575
How sweet is that?

172
00:11:09,416 --> 00:11:10,880
How sweet...

173
00:11:14,133 --> 00:11:15,805
When is he coming?

174
00:11:15,805 --> 00:11:18,366
He's taking the first train here tomorrow.

175
00:11:19,726 --> 00:11:23,482
I'll ask him to make me an omelet tomorrow.

176
00:11:24,115 --> 00:11:25,335
An omelet?

177
00:11:25,335 --> 00:11:26,610
From Ha Ru?

178
00:11:26,610 --> 00:11:27,775
Yeah.

179
00:11:27,775 --> 00:11:30,871
Remember? You loved them.
Said they were really good.

180
00:11:30,871 --> 00:11:32,645
Oh, yeah.

181
00:11:32,645 --> 00:11:36,727
Yoon Ha Ru... sure makes a great omelet.

182
00:11:38,188 --> 00:11:39,672
After Ha Ru injured his knee...

183
00:11:39,672 --> 00:11:42,206
and me, my shoulder, and we both quit judo...

184
00:11:42,206 --> 00:11:45,669
Everyone was worried about the two idiots
who knew nothing other than judo.

185
00:11:45,669 --> 00:11:49,421
But we both seem to have found our paths, no?

186
00:11:50,588 --> 00:11:51,924
Yeah.

187
00:11:51,924 --> 00:11:53,551
I guess so.

188
00:11:53,551 --> 00:11:56,215
Yoon Ha Ru has always been
passionate about food.

189
00:11:56,215 --> 00:11:58,642
Your father's a great cook, too.

190
00:11:58,642 --> 00:12:00,062
Maybe that's why,

191
00:12:00,062 --> 00:12:02,777
but he's clearly talented at cooking.

192
00:12:02,777 --> 00:12:05,941
I really do think he'd become a great chef.

193
00:12:14,192 --> 00:12:17,325
Where are we going?

194
00:12:17,325 --> 00:12:18,852
Home.

195
00:12:18,852 --> 00:12:20,156
Home?

196
00:12:20,833 --> 00:12:22,469
Your home?

197
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:25,787
Our... home.

198
00:12:26,529 --> 00:12:28,340
Our home?

199
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:29,662
Yeah.

200
00:12:30,913 --> 00:12:32,465
Right there.

201
00:12:33,544 --> 00:12:34,630
[Happy Home]

202
00:12:34,630 --> 00:12:36,728
<i>Wait, this is...</i>

203
00:12:36,728 --> 00:12:39,938
<i>the sharehouse that I lived in as a student!</i>

204
00:12:42,517 --> 00:12:44,432
Aren't you coming in?

205
00:12:44,432 --> 00:12:47,272
Yeah, I'm going in.

206
00:13:06,741 --> 00:13:08,183
[Happy Home]

207
00:13:10,714 --> 00:13:13,036
[Happy Home - Vacancy
Available immediately!]

208
00:13:28,327 --> 00:13:30,106
<i>It's just the same!</i>

209
00:13:30,106 --> 00:13:33,291
<i>This place hasn't changed a bit,
just as I remember.</i>

210
00:13:44,674 --> 00:13:46,163
[Jung Woo Jae]
[Yoon Ha Na]

211
00:13:55,279 --> 00:13:58,095
<i>She's acting a little strange today.</i>

212
00:13:58,760 --> 00:13:59,977
Ha Na.

213
00:13:59,977 --> 00:14:01,948
Mind if I shower first?

214
00:14:02,805 --> 00:14:05,214
Oh, go ahead.

215
00:14:17,274 --> 00:14:18,901
<i>What happened here?</i>

216
00:14:18,901 --> 00:14:20,226
<i>What is this?</i>

217
00:14:20,226 --> 00:14:21,890
<i>Am I...</i>

218
00:14:22,654 --> 00:14:25,124
<i>Am I living with Woo Jae?</i>

219
00:14:52,491 --> 00:14:54,300
[That Day's Warmth]
[World-famous star actress Yoon Ha Na]

220
00:14:55,937 --> 00:14:58,241
That's cringe!

221
00:14:59,953 --> 00:15:01,447
Wait a minute.

222
00:15:01,447 --> 00:15:02,949
If that's the case...

223
00:15:15,166 --> 00:15:17,190
This used to be Ha Ru's room...

224
00:15:17,190 --> 00:15:19,773
but now it's Woo Jae's, huh?

225
00:15:21,552 --> 00:15:22,653
Sorry, sorry.

226
00:15:22,653 --> 00:15:26,273
I just need to check something.
Just a moment will do.

227
00:15:35,917 --> 00:15:37,398
[Etiquette for the toilet]

228
00:15:55,455 --> 00:15:56,807
[Practical Theory of Security Services]

229
00:15:59,199 --> 00:16:00,556
Why...

230
00:16:00,556 --> 00:16:03,594
Why did it have to be security services?

231
00:16:13,644 --> 00:16:15,964
[6:00 AM - Wake up
6:30 AM - Breakfast...]

232
00:16:25,709 --> 00:16:29,118
<i>Well, something's changed, at least.</i>

233
00:16:29,118 --> 00:16:32,209
So that's why you joined the army back then.

234
00:16:32,209 --> 00:16:34,751
Because of your father's debt.

235
00:16:43,881 --> 00:16:46,927
<i>Sure, it's a shame
he's not in the national team,</i>

236
00:16:46,927 --> 00:16:49,024
<i>but this isn't half bad.</i>

237
00:16:49,024 --> 00:16:51,915
<i>I don't like that he's going to
become a bodyguard,</i>

238
00:16:51,915 --> 00:16:53,745
<i>but he's only 21.</i>

239
00:16:53,745 --> 00:16:56,738
<i>There's plenty of time to change things.</i>

240
00:16:57,375 --> 00:16:58,998
I can do this...

241
00:17:02,149 --> 00:17:04,331
Ha Na? What are you doing?

242
00:17:04,331 --> 00:17:06,989
Oh, I was...

243
00:17:06,989 --> 00:17:08,610
looking for my cup.

244
00:17:08,610 --> 00:17:09,825
I thought you might've used it.

245
00:17:09,825 --> 00:17:12,203
But it's not here.

246
00:17:12,203 --> 00:17:13,333
Check in Yoon Ha Ru's room.

247
00:17:13,333 --> 00:17:14,436
Yeah, Yoon Ha Ru.

248
00:17:14,436 --> 00:17:17,263
Never puts things back in place... yeah.

249
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:23,965
Are you hungry?

250
00:17:23,965 --> 00:17:25,368
No!

251
00:17:26,087 --> 00:17:28,719
Well, I could go for something.

252
00:17:28,719 --> 00:17:30,488
Want some ramyeon?

253
00:17:31,418 --> 00:17:36,082
Oh, yeah. If you want to.

254
00:17:36,712 --> 00:17:40,088
How about a beer to go with it?

255
00:17:40,088 --> 00:17:41,452
Sure.

256
00:17:54,590 --> 00:17:58,123
You're being so weird today, Ha Na.

257
00:17:58,123 --> 00:18:01,572
Oh, I'm just... happy.

258
00:18:02,354 --> 00:18:04,255
- About what?
- Us.

259
00:18:04,255 --> 00:18:05,977
- Huh?
- What?

260
00:18:10,594 --> 00:18:12,471
I mean, us,

261
00:18:12,471 --> 00:18:13,518
and this beer,

262
00:18:13,518 --> 00:18:16,726
and this ramyeon...

263
00:18:16,726 --> 00:18:19,865
This night, just good vibes, you know?

264
00:18:19,865 --> 00:18:22,460
You get me, don't you?

265
00:18:22,460 --> 00:18:24,150
I, well...

266
00:18:24,150 --> 00:18:26,332
Yeah, I guess.

267
00:18:39,413 --> 00:18:41,169
Anyway...

268
00:18:42,016 --> 00:18:44,842
Why do you want to become a bodyguard?

269
00:18:47,482 --> 00:18:49,191
I just...

270
00:18:52,094 --> 00:18:54,494
I have someone I want to protect.

271
00:19:01,182 --> 00:19:03,709
Let me go!

272
00:19:05,316 --> 00:19:06,525
What's this?

273
00:19:06,525 --> 00:19:07,846
Oh, Bi Gyeong!

274
00:19:07,846 --> 00:19:09,605
- And Soo Hyuk, too...
- Yeah, hi.

275
00:19:09,605 --> 00:19:12,244
How did the after-party go?

276
00:19:12,244 --> 00:19:14,898
She's really drunk.

277
00:19:14,898 --> 00:19:16,358
Cute.

278
00:19:16,358 --> 00:19:19,121
I mean, she's so drunk
she'll have to crawl upstairs.

279
00:19:19,121 --> 00:19:20,664
Yoon Ha Na.

280
00:19:20,664 --> 00:19:25,252
You left the party so early...

281
00:19:25,252 --> 00:19:27,421
and you're with Jung Woo Jae?

282
00:19:27,421 --> 00:19:30,174
Bi Gyeong, you must be tired.

283
00:19:30,174 --> 00:19:31,842
You must be exhausted, too, Ha Na.

284
00:19:31,842 --> 00:19:33,260
Should we wrap this up and call it a night?

285
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:34,970
- Oh, yeah.
- Good.

286
00:19:34,970 --> 00:19:37,825
Here, have a sip.

287
00:19:41,048 --> 00:19:43,687
Do you want to go upstairs? I can...

288
00:19:43,687 --> 00:19:45,940
Don't touch me!

289
00:19:45,940 --> 00:19:47,755
S-sorry.

290
00:19:48,566 --> 00:19:50,277
There we go.

291
00:19:50,277 --> 00:19:52,370
Let's go.

292
00:19:52,370 --> 00:19:54,657
Departing now!

293
00:19:54,657 --> 00:19:56,027
Stop!

294
00:19:57,201 --> 00:20:01,956
You little punks...
You go to sleep on time, you hear?

295
00:20:01,956 --> 00:20:03,791
I'll give you a proper scolding...

296
00:20:03,791 --> 00:20:05,835
- Yeah, sure...
- Go!

297
00:20:05,835 --> 00:20:07,586
Good night. Soo Hyuk, you did well.

298
00:20:07,586 --> 00:20:09,296
Yeah, good night!

299
00:20:09,296 --> 00:20:10,726
Go!

300
00:20:12,147 --> 00:20:14,212
- I'll clean up.
- Okay.

301
00:20:19,390 --> 00:20:21,790
<i>I have someone I want to protect.</i>

302
00:21:25,789 --> 00:21:28,459
Woo Jae, your form has
greatly improved since last year.

303
00:21:28,459 --> 00:21:29,919
You'd do great in practice.

304
00:21:29,919 --> 00:21:31,427
Thank you, sir.

305
00:21:33,464 --> 00:21:35,215
Let's have dinner sometime soon.

306
00:21:35,215 --> 00:21:36,550
Yes, sir.

307
00:21:36,550 --> 00:21:37,825
Next team!

308
00:21:37,825 --> 00:21:39,403
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

309
00:21:40,083 --> 00:21:42,181
[Creating a role]
Now...

310
00:21:42,181 --> 00:21:45,851
The first thing that
an actor should look for...

311
00:21:45,851 --> 00:21:49,521
is the character's dream.

312
00:21:49,521 --> 00:21:53,525
Something that burns hot in their chest.

313
00:21:53,525 --> 00:21:55,925
Also called a super-objective.

314
00:21:58,072 --> 00:22:01,492
An actor is someone
who dives into a character's life,

315
00:22:01,492 --> 00:22:04,742
and rewrites their fate.

316
00:22:05,871 --> 00:22:09,083
If one loves the role more than anyone else,

317
00:22:09,083 --> 00:22:11,914
- they, by themselves...
<i>- Going to the past isn't what swaps our bodies,</i>

318
00:22:11,914 --> 00:22:14,935
<i>but we swap each time we time travel.</i>

319
00:22:14,935 --> 00:22:17,490
<i>Which means, if we go back to the present now,</i>

320
00:22:17,490 --> 00:22:19,705
<i>I'll be Yoon Ha Ru again!</i>

321
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,955
[2026: Present]

322
00:22:26,950 --> 00:22:31,294
<i>Come to think of it,
we've only returned to the present once.</i>

323
00:22:31,294 --> 00:22:35,925
<i>We're not stuck like this,
lost in the past, are we?</i>

324
00:22:35,925 --> 00:22:38,649
[Time travel: body change]
<i>We've been jumping so much.</i>

325
00:22:38,649 --> 00:22:41,494
<i>So why can't I figure out the pattern?</i>

326
00:22:50,969 --> 00:22:52,031
So handsome!

327
00:22:52,031 --> 00:22:53,605
- Look at his nose! So sharp!
- Unreal.

328
00:22:53,605 --> 00:22:54,634
Did you see that?

329
00:22:54,634 --> 00:22:56,973
- This can't be real.
- So good-looking!

330
00:22:56,973 --> 00:22:58,086
How does he do it?

331
00:22:58,086 --> 00:22:59,713
He goes to our school?

332
00:22:59,713 --> 00:23:01,343
- So handsome!
- Who is that?

333
00:23:01,343 --> 00:23:03,717
No way he goes to our school.

334
00:23:03,717 --> 00:23:05,305
He's so handsome!

335
00:23:05,305 --> 00:23:07,438
He's just my type!

336
00:23:08,589 --> 00:23:10,281
- He's glowing!
- Oh, what do I do?

337
00:23:10,281 --> 00:23:11,589
Just as I expected...

338
00:23:11,589 --> 00:23:15,040
The judo player Yoon Ha Ru may be lost in time,

339
00:23:15,749 --> 00:23:19,300
but my charming presence
overthrows the fabric of time and space.

340
00:23:23,657 --> 00:23:25,401
Grab him.

341
00:23:29,163 --> 00:23:30,475
Who's that?

342
00:23:31,165 --> 00:23:32,458
Hey.

343
00:23:33,167 --> 00:23:35,791
Time's up. Why are you still here?

344
00:23:40,215 --> 00:23:41,739
Wait, then.

345
00:23:43,093 --> 00:23:44,678
Our national player is still wrapping up.

346
00:23:44,678 --> 00:23:46,870
So, what's he doing?

347
00:23:46,870 --> 00:23:48,766
It looks to me like he's sleeping.

348
00:23:48,766 --> 00:23:50,934
It's the rule to clear out
five minutes before practice.

349
00:23:50,934 --> 00:23:52,683
We need to practice.

350
00:23:52,683 --> 00:23:54,188
So clear out. Now.

351
00:23:54,188 --> 00:23:56,523
What do you even practice with?

352
00:23:56,523 --> 00:23:59,276
Do you play tag or something?

353
00:23:59,276 --> 00:24:01,836
What did you say? Say it again.

354
00:24:01,836 --> 00:24:03,247
Hey!

355
00:24:07,576 --> 00:24:09,490
What's all this noise about?

356
00:24:24,259 --> 00:24:26,095
Stick to the rules.

357
00:24:26,095 --> 00:24:28,671
Oh, my bad.

358
00:24:32,935 --> 00:24:35,698
Guess all the judo dropouts like to
huddle up in security services.

359
00:24:35,698 --> 00:24:37,166
You little...

360
00:24:43,442 --> 00:24:46,385
Are your classes treating you well?

361
00:24:46,385 --> 00:24:47,712
Yeah.

362
00:24:49,011 --> 00:24:50,885
I see.

363
00:24:52,417 --> 00:24:54,325
That's good to hear.

364
00:24:57,164 --> 00:24:58,843
Aren't you leaving?

365
00:25:00,337 --> 00:25:02,359
I am.

366
00:25:02,359 --> 00:25:03,711
Don't fret.

367
00:25:04,716 --> 00:25:07,242
Guys! Let's move!

368
00:25:07,242 --> 00:25:08,745
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

369
00:25:12,611 --> 00:25:14,935
Wow, what a joke.

370
00:25:14,935 --> 00:25:18,128
Are we just going to let them be?

371
00:25:18,128 --> 00:25:20,528
You'd beat him in 3 seconds tops!

372
00:25:23,485 --> 00:25:25,154
It's fine.

373
00:25:25,154 --> 00:25:26,363
Let's just get ready for practice.

374
00:25:26,363 --> 00:25:28,738
- Hey, you. Come here!
- Let's not, okay?

375
00:25:28,738 --> 00:25:30,951
Let me at them. Hey!

376
00:25:30,951 --> 00:25:32,993
That's it for today.

377
00:25:32,993 --> 00:25:34,145
See you next class.

378
00:25:34,145 --> 00:25:36,962
- Yes, ma'am!
- Good work, everyone!

379
00:25:38,667 --> 00:25:41,798
Do you want to go eat something?

380
00:25:41,798 --> 00:25:44,375
- Yeah, let's go.
- Yeah!

381
00:25:45,132 --> 00:25:46,800
Guys, wait just a second!

382
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:48,655
Just a moment.

383
00:25:48,655 --> 00:25:51,221
The casting results
for the short film are here.

384
00:25:51,221 --> 00:25:53,390
We've confirmed with the professor.

385
00:25:53,390 --> 00:25:56,134
We'll start with the female lead.

386
00:25:56,134 --> 00:25:59,429
<i>The short film competition in 2013...</i>

387
00:26:00,631 --> 00:26:03,095
<i>The female lead, So Hee, goes to...</i>

388
00:26:03,095 --> 00:26:04,359
<i>Yoon Ha Na.</i>

389
00:26:04,359 --> 00:26:06,757
<i>Of course, the female lead is Yoon Ha Na.</i>

390
00:26:06,757 --> 00:26:09,821
<i>Your face has such good coherence.</i>

391
00:26:09,821 --> 00:26:12,201
<i>As for the lens...</i>

392
00:26:12,201 --> 00:26:14,431
<i>A '60s Carl Zeiss. That would do nicely.</i>

393
00:26:14,431 --> 00:26:16,519
<i>- Congrats.
- Haesol's pride!</i>

394
00:26:16,519 --> 00:26:19,082
<i>Haesol's princess, Yoon Ha Na!</i>

395
00:26:19,082 --> 00:26:22,113
<i>- Thank you.
- You need to be the sturdy centerpiece.</i>

396
00:26:22,113 --> 00:26:23,916
<i>- Got it?
- Yes!</i>

397
00:26:25,281 --> 00:26:27,504
The female lead, So Hee, goes to...

398
00:26:27,504 --> 00:26:29,026
Please, please...

399
00:26:31,595 --> 00:26:33,118
Yoon Ha Na.

400
00:26:37,017 --> 00:26:40,062
Of course the female lead is Yoon Ha Na.

401
00:26:40,062 --> 00:26:43,565
Your face has such good coherence.

402
00:26:43,565 --> 00:26:46,443
As for the lens...

403
00:26:46,443 --> 00:26:49,988
A '60s Carl Zeiss. That would do nicely.

404
00:26:49,988 --> 00:26:51,323
Wow.

405
00:26:51,323 --> 00:26:52,866
Look at Ha Na.

406
00:26:52,866 --> 00:26:54,618
Not even a blink, huh?

407
00:26:54,618 --> 00:26:57,019
- Congrats.
- Congratulations, Ha Na!

408
00:26:57,019 --> 00:27:00,132
Haesol's pride, Haesol's princess, Yoon Ha Na!

409
00:27:05,080 --> 00:27:08,298
You need to be the sturdy centerpiece, got it?

410
00:27:08,298 --> 00:27:10,259
The professor said
that you're the one for this role.

411
00:27:10,259 --> 00:27:12,686
Oh, of course.

412
00:27:12,686 --> 00:27:15,222
<i>This film won four awards
at the Busan International Film Festival.</i>

413
00:27:15,222 --> 00:27:17,724
<i>Jun Mo won Best New Director
at the Grand Bell Awards,</i>

414
00:27:17,724 --> 00:27:19,863
<i>and I won Best New Female Lead.</i>

415
00:27:19,863 --> 00:27:24,481
<i>It was invited to overseas film festivals
and gained a lot of traction, too.</i>

416
00:27:24,481 --> 00:27:25,924
<i>Thank you, Jun Mo.</i>

417
00:27:25,924 --> 00:27:29,985
<i>Your persona, Yoon Ha Na's life...
is back in motion.</i>

418
00:27:30,696 --> 00:27:33,314
As for the male lead...

419
00:27:34,533 --> 00:27:36,193
it's yet to be announced.

420
00:27:37,077 --> 00:27:38,545
As you all know,

421
00:27:38,545 --> 00:27:41,123
this role doesn't talk a lot
but instead puts weight on action scenes.

422
00:27:41,123 --> 00:27:42,788
Which is why I think...

423
00:27:42,788 --> 00:27:44,574
maybe we should widen our search.

424
00:27:44,574 --> 00:27:47,481
Get applicants from other departments, too.

425
00:27:48,955 --> 00:27:53,151
<i>I remember a complete amateur
phys. ed student ended up as the male lead.</i>

426
00:27:53,151 --> 00:27:54,516
<i>Wait.</i>

427
00:27:54,516 --> 00:27:57,962
<i>What if Woo Jae wasn't a bodyguard,
but an actor?</i>

428
00:27:57,962 --> 00:28:00,133
<i>What if he wasn't the protector,</i>

429
00:28:00,133 --> 00:28:02,527
<i>but became someone who gets protected?</i>

430
00:28:02,527 --> 00:28:04,646
<i>Physically adept, action-ready,</i>

431
00:28:04,646 --> 00:28:08,375
<i>and a dramatic look in the eyes, you get me?</i>

432
00:28:09,443 --> 00:28:11,320
- Ha Na? Anything to add?
- Jun Mo!

433
00:28:11,320 --> 00:28:14,663
Physically adept, action-ready,
and a dramatic look in the eyes, right?

434
00:28:18,127 --> 00:28:19,667
Yoon Ha Na...

435
00:28:20,409 --> 00:28:22,536
That's what I was about to say.
Did you just read my mind?

436
00:28:22,536 --> 00:28:23,619
You're creeping me out!

437
00:28:23,619 --> 00:28:26,873
A tall-as-a-door male lead with
a whole story to tell with his back, right?

438
00:28:26,873 --> 00:28:30,380
I guess... I understand
what half of that means.

439
00:28:30,380 --> 00:28:32,956
What do you mean, "tall-as-a-door?"

440
00:28:35,403 --> 00:28:39,222
Like, someone with
an overwhelming physical presence,

441
00:28:39,222 --> 00:28:44,718
and is a heartthrob
at the same time and tall...

442
00:28:45,479 --> 00:28:48,065
is what they call... people like that.

443
00:28:48,065 --> 00:28:50,567
I think.

444
00:28:50,567 --> 00:28:52,361
Who says that?

445
00:28:52,361 --> 00:28:55,322
I guess it's one of those trendy new words.

446
00:28:55,322 --> 00:28:58,488
- Like, "hot stuff" or "ripped chad."
- Yeah.

447
00:28:58,488 --> 00:29:00,702
Something like that, probably.

448
00:29:00,702 --> 00:29:01,912
What are you all amazed about?

449
00:29:01,912 --> 00:29:05,207
Kids these days with their nonsense words!

450
00:29:05,207 --> 00:29:06,708
Say, "he's well-built,"

451
00:29:06,708 --> 00:29:09,086
"he's strong and handsome,"

452
00:29:09,086 --> 00:29:10,462
or "he's built like a warrior."

453
00:29:10,462 --> 00:29:13,048
See all these perfectly good ways
to describe someone?

454
00:29:13,048 --> 00:29:15,467
It's just all too much...

455
00:29:15,467 --> 00:29:18,345
It's a bit much. Right, Jun Mo?

456
00:29:18,345 --> 00:29:20,055
I agree.

457
00:29:20,055 --> 00:29:21,848
That's the kind of male lead I want.

458
00:29:21,848 --> 00:29:23,266
"Tall-as-a-door!"

459
00:29:23,266 --> 00:29:24,935
- Okay.
- Yeah, okay.

460
00:29:24,935 --> 00:29:27,634
Hey, Ha Na.

461
00:29:29,733 --> 00:29:31,773
Can we leave, too?

462
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:41,964
[Yoon Ha Na]
<i>I'm here. Come out.</i>

463
00:29:52,597 --> 00:29:54,098
Seo Ye Rang?

464
00:30:03,929 --> 00:30:06,309
I lost again...

465
00:30:06,309 --> 00:30:08,979
Why can't I win just once?

466
00:30:08,979 --> 00:30:13,233
I stayed up all night practicing
a thousand times, so why...

467
00:30:13,233 --> 00:30:15,999
Why can't Seo Ye Rang win against Yoon Ha Na?

468
00:30:15,999 --> 00:30:18,758
Wow, she's always been this mad.

469
00:30:18,758 --> 00:30:21,540
Everyone's lying when they say
working hard is also a talent.

470
00:30:23,034 --> 00:30:24,892
It's honestly a curse!

471
00:30:24,892 --> 00:30:27,028
Just futile hope.

472
00:30:30,193 --> 00:30:32,184
Don't cry, Seo Ye Rang.

473
00:30:33,295 --> 00:30:35,046
Keep your head up high, Seo Ye Rang.

474
00:30:35,046 --> 00:30:36,440
She's crying?

475
00:30:36,440 --> 00:30:38,147
Seo Ye Rang is crying?

476
00:30:41,428 --> 00:30:43,542
<i>Why are you crying?</i>

477
00:30:47,392 --> 00:30:49,273
<i>Oh, it's you, Yoon Ha Ru...</i>

478
00:30:50,774 --> 00:30:53,688
<i>I don't know...</i>

479
00:31:02,115 --> 00:31:04,364
<i>I want to be good, too...</i>

480
00:31:05,783 --> 00:31:07,403
<i>Oh, this is the moment!</i>

481
00:31:07,403 --> 00:31:11,374
<i>- This is when I first met her.</i>
- I hate everything!

482
00:31:11,374 --> 00:31:13,752
Who did it? Who did this to you?

483
00:31:13,752 --> 00:31:15,795
- What the hell?
- Who did this?

484
00:31:15,795 --> 00:31:18,173
Which bastard was it? Just say the word!

485
00:31:18,173 --> 00:31:20,300
I'll take care of...

486
00:31:20,300 --> 00:31:23,221
I'll do things! Yeah!

487
00:31:24,471 --> 00:31:25,978
Excuse me...

488
00:31:28,353 --> 00:31:29,859
What are you doing?

489
00:31:29,859 --> 00:31:31,093
What?

490
00:31:33,563 --> 00:31:35,075
Wait, something's wrong.

491
00:31:36,815 --> 00:31:38,852
Why aren't you cuddling up to me?

492
00:31:39,583 --> 00:31:40,825
What?

493
00:31:40,825 --> 00:31:46,108
Did you really just ask me...
why I'm not cuddling you?

494
00:31:47,869 --> 00:31:51,863
What am I supposed to think of
this borderline-innovative-loon?

495
00:31:53,917 --> 00:31:56,336
You're just so cute, Seo Ye Rang.

496
00:31:56,336 --> 00:31:57,837
What?

497
00:31:57,837 --> 00:32:01,082
How do you know my name?
I've never seen you before.

498
00:32:02,050 --> 00:32:05,983
Who the heck are you?

499
00:32:11,935 --> 00:32:14,086
<i>Babe, it's me...</i>

500
00:32:14,086 --> 00:32:18,185
<i>It's Yoon Ha Ru, whom you had
a debilitating crush on back then.</i>

501
00:32:25,115 --> 00:32:27,284
Are you a student here?

502
00:32:27,284 --> 00:32:30,537
Class of 2013, culinary arts.

503
00:32:30,537 --> 00:32:32,330
- How old?
- 30...

504
00:32:32,330 --> 00:32:35,652
I mean, 21.

505
00:32:35,652 --> 00:32:39,429
You rude little thing,
how dare you talk to me like that?

506
00:32:40,714 --> 00:32:43,967
<i>I guess you've always been aggressive, babe...</i>

507
00:32:43,967 --> 00:32:45,552
You!

508
00:32:45,552 --> 00:32:48,430
I'll let you off easy this time,
because I feel sorry for your delusional head,

509
00:32:48,430 --> 00:32:50,164
but if I ever cross paths with you again,

510
00:32:50,164 --> 00:32:53,493
I'll show you what true aggression is.

511
00:32:53,493 --> 00:32:55,936
So you'd better watch where you're going.

512
00:32:55,936 --> 00:32:57,521
Ugh, I should just...

513
00:32:58,607 --> 00:33:01,880
I'm pissed off already, I can't deal with this.

514
00:33:03,069 --> 00:33:04,195
Why?

515
00:33:04,195 --> 00:33:07,282
Why hasn't she fallen in love with me?

516
00:33:07,282 --> 00:33:08,491
Why?

517
00:33:08,491 --> 00:33:12,370
But I look good today!

518
00:33:12,370 --> 00:33:13,769
Why?

519
00:33:29,005 --> 00:33:30,851
- Hi.
- Gosh, you scared me!

520
00:33:34,309 --> 00:33:35,974
There you are.

521
00:33:37,687 --> 00:33:39,939
Look who's grumpy.

522
00:33:39,939 --> 00:33:42,430
You're so ugly when you frown.

523
00:33:42,430 --> 00:33:45,028
I'm sorry, Yoon Ha Ru.

524
00:33:45,028 --> 00:33:46,887
This is all my fault.

525
00:33:46,887 --> 00:33:50,090
If only I didn't get you injured...

526
00:33:51,195 --> 00:33:53,161
Oh, you're moping again.

527
00:33:53,161 --> 00:33:56,206
Hey, if I'm being honest,
I've had my fair share of judo.

528
00:33:56,206 --> 00:33:59,459
No, not even that. I was getting sick of it.

529
00:33:59,459 --> 00:34:03,922
From primary school up until
I reached 33, that's a long 22 years.

530
00:34:03,922 --> 00:34:05,840
I've won every color of every medal.

531
00:34:05,840 --> 00:34:08,551
And I already made my way to the top.
Global ranking number one.

532
00:34:08,551 --> 00:34:10,818
What makes you think I have
unfinished business with my judo journey?

533
00:34:10,818 --> 00:34:14,974
I would've had my pants
in a knot anyway after retiring.

534
00:34:14,974 --> 00:34:16,223
Honestly, this is better.

535
00:34:16,223 --> 00:34:20,939
Yoon Ha Ru, who's already
had the world under his thumb, still 21?

536
00:34:20,939 --> 00:34:24,117
I've got so much potential. Yes, I do!

537
00:34:25,068 --> 00:34:26,640
But...

538
00:34:27,386 --> 00:34:29,489
You know what I always think?

539
00:34:29,489 --> 00:34:31,950
You have a tendency to... underestimate me.

540
00:34:31,950 --> 00:34:33,576
You think less of me, don't you?

541
00:34:33,576 --> 00:34:35,713
When did I do that?

542
00:34:35,713 --> 00:34:37,747
If Yoon Ha Ru made a choice at 20 years old,

543
00:34:37,747 --> 00:34:39,585
he must've had a good reason.

544
00:34:39,585 --> 00:34:41,209
I trust in him.

545
00:34:41,209 --> 00:34:43,795
That's why I'll support his choice.

546
00:34:43,795 --> 00:34:46,631
You should trust in me, too, and support me!

547
00:34:46,631 --> 00:34:49,101
So what's that reason of yours?

548
00:34:49,101 --> 00:34:51,469
That's, well...

549
00:34:51,469 --> 00:34:53,615
That's for us to find out.

550
00:34:55,762 --> 00:34:58,719
You'll muck up your luck
if you keep making that face.

551
00:35:00,979 --> 00:35:03,308
So, what should we do with Jung Woo Jae?

552
00:35:03,308 --> 00:35:05,442
What's his deal?
Was he your guard dog in a past life?

553
00:35:05,442 --> 00:35:06,943
Why is he so dead set on protecting you?

554
00:35:06,943 --> 00:35:08,554
Is that his life's calling, or what?

555
00:35:08,554 --> 00:35:10,196
Speaking of...

556
00:35:10,196 --> 00:35:12,615
Why are you all serious now?
You're freaking me out.

557
00:35:12,615 --> 00:35:14,909
I'm going to make Woo Jae an actor.

558
00:35:14,909 --> 00:35:16,884
- An actor?
- Yeah.

559
00:35:17,495 --> 00:35:19,873
Does he want to?

560
00:35:19,873 --> 00:35:22,372
We'll make him!

561
00:35:23,209 --> 00:35:25,420
- We?
- Well...

562
00:35:27,797 --> 00:35:29,591
You don't have to help.

563
00:35:29,591 --> 00:35:32,302
It's not like you to back down like that.

564
00:35:32,302 --> 00:35:34,771
We can try and make it work. Why not?

565
00:35:34,771 --> 00:35:36,014
Really?

566
00:35:36,014 --> 00:35:38,924
He's my friend, too, you know.

567
00:35:44,230 --> 00:35:46,816
- Such a manly body...
- But he's got a baby face!

568
00:35:46,816 --> 00:35:49,354
- As cool as a breeze...
- But as hot as the sun!

569
00:35:49,354 --> 00:35:51,416
I can't believe you're real...

570
00:35:51,416 --> 00:35:53,948
I'm going to become a fan.

571
00:35:53,948 --> 00:35:56,384
This is you, right?

572
00:35:58,745 --> 00:36:03,458
I guess that's me, but... What's this about?

573
00:36:03,458 --> 00:36:04,834
Nice to meet you!

574
00:36:04,834 --> 00:36:06,961
We saw this and we instantly knew it.

575
00:36:06,961 --> 00:36:07,987
Knew what?

576
00:36:07,987 --> 00:36:09,756
You already belong to the public.

577
00:36:09,756 --> 00:36:12,133
It's time for the whole country
to fall in love with you!

578
00:36:12,133 --> 00:36:13,718
Absolute heartthrob.

579
00:36:13,718 --> 00:36:16,137
You're the most handsome guy I've ever seen.

580
00:36:16,137 --> 00:36:18,672
You're so, so, so cool!

581
00:36:20,058 --> 00:36:21,684
Which is why we made this.

582
00:36:21,684 --> 00:36:23,728
Ta-da!

583
00:36:23,728 --> 00:36:26,397
[We will protect Jung Woo Jae!]
Our day one has already started!

584
00:36:26,397 --> 00:36:30,398
- What?
- We, the Woo Jae Guardians, will protect you!

585
00:36:36,819 --> 00:36:39,950
I have to get to practice,
so if you'll excuse me...

586
00:36:39,950 --> 00:36:42,997
- Oh, yeah, of course!
- Right, uh, please, take this.

587
00:36:42,997 --> 00:36:44,916
Right, thank you.

588
00:36:44,916 --> 00:36:46,866
He's popular.

589
00:36:46,866 --> 00:36:48,169
Yeah, no joke.

590
00:36:48,169 --> 00:36:50,673
He's... very popular.

591
00:36:50,673 --> 00:36:53,251
- Bye!
- Hey, we're leaving.

592
00:36:53,251 --> 00:36:56,344
Hey, Woo Jae. Hear that?
You're "public domain."

593
00:36:56,344 --> 00:36:58,448
Stop teasing me. They're just poking fun.

594
00:36:58,448 --> 00:37:00,475
Doesn't seem that way to me.

595
00:37:01,180 --> 00:37:03,123
The "Woo Jae Guardians?"

596
00:37:03,726 --> 00:37:05,803
Well, I'm convinced.

597
00:37:05,803 --> 00:37:08,067
The whole country will fall in love with you.

598
00:37:08,067 --> 00:37:10,483
Cut it out, Yoon Ha Ru.

599
00:37:10,483 --> 00:37:12,026
I still have another session.

600
00:37:12,026 --> 00:37:13,194
See you at home.

601
00:37:13,194 --> 00:37:15,595
- Okay, good luck at practice!
- Thanks.

602
00:37:15,595 --> 00:37:18,026
Oh, you want this?

603
00:37:18,697 --> 00:37:19,888
Yes.

604
00:37:20,535 --> 00:37:22,203
I'll be going, then.

605
00:37:22,203 --> 00:37:24,122
- Bye!
- See you!

606
00:37:24,122 --> 00:37:26,332
Bye!

607
00:37:26,332 --> 00:37:28,042
- We love you!
- Goodbye!

608
00:37:28,042 --> 00:37:29,335
Love you!

609
00:37:29,335 --> 00:37:31,892
- Bye!
- Take care!

610
00:37:33,033 --> 00:37:34,490
- Is that his girlfriend?
- That was unreal!

611
00:37:34,490 --> 00:37:35,839
He's so tall!

612
00:37:35,839 --> 00:37:38,653
- I think I've fallen for him again!
- So handsome!

613
00:37:39,971 --> 00:37:41,639
That's not how love works.

614
00:37:41,639 --> 00:37:43,264
Hey, you can have this.

615
00:37:43,264 --> 00:37:45,101
Okay...

616
00:37:45,101 --> 00:37:46,895
Those little brats, they're basically children!

617
00:37:46,895 --> 00:37:48,412
I'd like for that to happen to me...

618
00:37:48,412 --> 00:37:50,778
What's with their heights, too?

619
00:37:53,392 --> 00:37:55,232
You sure you'll be alright?

620
00:37:55,862 --> 00:37:57,030
What do you mean?

621
00:37:57,030 --> 00:38:00,852
Just one video online,
and now he's got a fan club.

622
00:38:00,852 --> 00:38:01,877
Once he becomes an actor,

623
00:38:01,877 --> 00:38:04,370
there'll be a line of girls
wanting to get with him.

624
00:38:04,370 --> 00:38:07,665
Would you be able to deal with that?

625
00:38:07,665 --> 00:38:08,875
What're you yapping for?

626
00:38:08,875 --> 00:38:11,252
Hey, I'm Yoon Ha Na.

627
00:38:11,252 --> 00:38:13,369
Crowned Best Actress at Baekryong,
every Gen Z's wannabe role model!

628
00:38:13,369 --> 00:38:17,091
The icon of sold-out tickets, the undefeated
"most datable celeb," Yoon Ha Na!

629
00:38:17,091 --> 00:38:18,343
Got it?

630
00:38:18,343 --> 00:38:21,051
It doesn't bother me one bit.

631
00:38:25,016 --> 00:38:28,561
I see that only four measly "Woo Jae Guardians"
have completely broken you.

632
00:38:28,561 --> 00:38:30,772
Your face is a sight to see.

633
00:38:30,772 --> 00:38:32,529
Shut it.

634
00:38:35,652 --> 00:38:38,321
So, you've seen it now. He's got potential.

635
00:38:38,321 --> 00:38:40,162
I can feel that something's brewing.

636
00:38:40,162 --> 00:38:43,868
I don't think we should
let this opportunity pass us by.

637
00:38:43,868 --> 00:38:45,586
And opportunities are best when seized.

638
00:38:45,586 --> 00:38:47,116
A bit of skill and a lot of luck go a long way.

639
00:38:47,116 --> 00:38:49,868
It's all about the right timing. This time...

640
00:38:50,959 --> 00:38:54,379
He won't have anyone's back,
but instead, he'll be standing up front.

641
00:38:54,379 --> 00:38:57,187
Alright. So, what's next?

642
00:39:00,596 --> 00:39:03,638
So you have a plan!

643
00:39:03,638 --> 00:39:05,597
Let me hear it, too!

644
00:39:05,597 --> 00:39:08,007
Come on, just a hint!

645
00:39:11,249 --> 00:39:12,274
Hey, try it out.

646
00:39:12,274 --> 00:39:13,591
["That Summer, Us" Male Lead Audition]
Sounds like fun.

647
00:39:13,591 --> 00:39:16,933
Wait, the class of 2008 is Yang Jun Mo's class!

648
00:39:16,933 --> 00:39:19,240
- Let's go.
- Okay.

649
00:39:22,406 --> 00:39:24,737
["That Summer, Us" Male Lead Audition]

650
00:39:24,737 --> 00:39:26,929
[Any student at Yongwon University may apply.
No prior acting experience needed.]

651
00:39:40,341 --> 00:39:41,801
Don't give it away, okay? Act natural.

652
00:39:41,801 --> 00:39:43,928
He's quick to pick up on things, you know.

653
00:39:43,928 --> 00:39:47,223
Would you stop worrying? Just trust me.

654
00:39:47,223 --> 00:39:51,060
People suggested that I become
a child actor when I was little and stuff.

655
00:39:51,060 --> 00:39:53,151
- Shut up.
- I swear!

656
00:39:53,896 --> 00:39:57,817
Oh! What is this?

657
00:39:57,817 --> 00:39:59,318
Glad you asked!

658
00:39:59,318 --> 00:40:01,946
It's a short film that I'm going to be in.

659
00:40:01,946 --> 00:40:04,992
But we don't have a good male lead,
so there's going to be an audition.

660
00:40:04,992 --> 00:40:06,642
Really?

661
00:40:06,642 --> 00:40:10,246
This could be the path to fame!

662
00:40:10,246 --> 00:40:12,457
Maybe I should give it a shot?

663
00:40:12,457 --> 00:40:14,500
You could!

664
00:40:14,500 --> 00:40:17,795
Anyone can apply! It's a free audition.

665
00:40:17,795 --> 00:40:18,921
An audition?

666
00:40:18,921 --> 00:40:22,467
I see!

667
00:40:22,467 --> 00:40:26,207
Jung Woo Jae, why don't you give it a shot?

668
00:40:26,207 --> 00:40:27,513
Me?

669
00:40:27,513 --> 00:40:29,390
No way, I can't do that.

670
00:40:29,390 --> 00:40:32,540
Why not? Physically adept, action-ready,
and a dramatic look in the eyes. That's you!

671
00:40:32,540 --> 00:40:33,895
That's you!

672
00:40:33,895 --> 00:40:35,063
Oh, no.

673
00:40:35,063 --> 00:40:37,065
An overwhelming physical presence,
who's also a heartthrob!

674
00:40:37,065 --> 00:40:40,184
There's no denying it, you fit the bill!

675
00:40:40,184 --> 00:40:41,628
You!

676
00:40:42,321 --> 00:40:44,388
A heartthrob?

677
00:40:44,388 --> 00:40:45,597
Me?

678
00:40:46,407 --> 00:40:49,410
I mean...

679
00:40:49,410 --> 00:40:51,329
The Woo Jae Guardians,
they seemed to think that.

680
00:40:51,329 --> 00:40:52,621
Ba-dump, ba-dump.

681
00:40:52,621 --> 00:40:54,329
Pit-a-pat.

682
00:40:56,357 --> 00:40:57,668
No way.

683
00:40:57,668 --> 00:40:59,532
I don't know how to act.

684
00:41:06,427 --> 00:41:08,304
This is all because your acting sucked!

685
00:41:08,304 --> 00:41:11,099
What? I thought I did amazing!

686
00:41:11,099 --> 00:41:13,643
Woo Jae, the male lead role's name is Gang Ho.

687
00:41:13,643 --> 00:41:16,270
"Gang Ho," because
he's such a gangster, and hot!

688
00:41:16,270 --> 00:41:19,772
Please, just read the script! Just once!

689
00:41:25,149 --> 00:41:27,198
The male lead role's name is Gang Ho.

690
00:41:27,198 --> 00:41:29,784
"Gang Ho," because
he's such a gangster, and hot!

691
00:41:29,784 --> 00:41:33,352
Please, just read the script, just once!

692
00:41:36,916 --> 00:41:39,085
- Ha Na...
- Woo Jae.

693
00:41:39,085 --> 00:41:41,504
Life is a drama, and you're the main actor.

694
00:41:41,504 --> 00:41:43,131
Let's quit being Woo Jae the bodyguard,

695
00:41:43,131 --> 00:41:45,299
and write an awesome fantasy with me!

696
00:41:45,299 --> 00:41:47,960
You'll be Jung Woo Jae, a worldwide star!

697
00:41:48,761 --> 00:41:50,972
But Ha Na...

698
00:41:50,972 --> 00:41:53,391
My life is more like a documentary.

699
00:41:53,391 --> 00:41:55,473
Not a fantasy.

700
00:41:56,519 --> 00:41:58,980
See you at home. Bye.

701
00:41:58,980 --> 00:42:01,006
Your face is already a fantasy!

702
00:42:01,006 --> 00:42:04,726
You should be charged guilty
for not putting your looks to use!

703
00:42:18,933 --> 00:42:20,554
Yoon Ha Na! Hi!

704
00:42:20,554 --> 00:42:23,294
How's your movie going?

705
00:42:23,294 --> 00:42:25,381
Oh, the movie...

706
00:42:25,381 --> 00:42:29,802
I don't know, it might get scrapped because
a certain someone won't play the male lead.

707
00:42:29,802 --> 00:42:31,179
Oh, my!

708
00:42:31,179 --> 00:42:35,016
What a disaster, oh, no!

709
00:42:39,521 --> 00:42:43,403
Oh, these awesome lines and beautiful scenes...

710
00:42:43,403 --> 00:42:47,195
I really hoped to let the world see this...

711
00:42:47,195 --> 00:42:50,669
How I wish upon the stars
for someone to play the male lead!

712
00:42:52,867 --> 00:42:55,119
- Ha Na.
- Yeah? Why? You'll do it?

713
00:42:55,119 --> 00:42:56,749
No, well...

714
00:42:56,749 --> 00:42:59,349
You're holding the script upside down.

715
00:43:04,462 --> 00:43:06,164
Whatever.

716
00:43:14,597 --> 00:43:17,944
I'll apply for the audition, but that's it.

717
00:43:19,504 --> 00:43:20,537
Really?

718
00:43:20,537 --> 00:43:23,864
You promise, Woo Jae? You'll do it?

719
00:43:24,897 --> 00:43:27,068
Don't get your hopes up.

720
00:43:27,068 --> 00:43:29,468
- I won't make it.
- Oh, yeah!

721
00:43:29,468 --> 00:43:31,791
I mean, you'll make it!

722
00:43:37,870 --> 00:43:39,646
Do you want to see the script?

723
00:43:48,464 --> 00:43:50,383
Good, now turn the light up.

724
00:43:50,383 --> 00:43:52,106
Straighten that banner out!

725
00:43:52,106 --> 00:43:53,803
[That Summer, Us]

726
00:43:53,803 --> 00:43:54,971
Is that good? More.

727
00:43:54,971 --> 00:43:56,138
To the right!

728
00:43:56,138 --> 00:43:57,431
That's good!

729
00:43:57,431 --> 00:44:00,738
Okay, that's good.

730
00:44:03,751 --> 00:44:05,975
["That Summer, Us" Male Lead Audition]

731
00:44:14,573 --> 00:44:17,434
Kim Jun Woo, physical education, class of 2013.

732
00:44:17,434 --> 00:44:20,013
- Here.
- This way. Follow me.

733
00:44:27,628 --> 00:44:31,618
Hello, everyone!
This is Kim Jun Woo, class of 2013!

734
00:44:45,104 --> 00:44:48,107
Hello! I'm Gang Li Ho, class of 2013!

735
00:44:48,107 --> 00:44:51,435
I'll demonstrate my shadowboxing skills!

736
00:45:04,665 --> 00:45:07,585
Hi, everyone!
I'm Kim Seong Hoon, class of 2013!

737
00:45:07,585 --> 00:45:09,298
I'll be singing a song today!

738
00:45:09,298 --> 00:45:12,291
<i>♪ Our paths may diverge time and time again ♪</i>

739
00:45:12,291 --> 00:45:14,855
<i>♪ But I'll still wait for you ♪</i>

740
00:45:14,855 --> 00:45:17,426
<i>♪ My heart may break beyond repair ♪</i>

741
00:45:17,426 --> 00:45:19,970
<i>♪ But I'll still smile for you ♪</i>

742
00:45:19,970 --> 00:45:22,156
<i>♪ I may turn away... ♪</i>

743
00:45:23,768 --> 00:45:25,478
I'm sorry.

744
00:45:25,478 --> 00:45:28,647
I don't think this is working at all.

745
00:45:28,647 --> 00:45:30,528
Get him out of here.

746
00:45:35,603 --> 00:45:37,073
Greetings, everyone!

747
00:45:37,073 --> 00:45:41,200
I'm Han Soo Hyuk, the film department's
cutie-patootie, class of 2013!

748
00:45:41,200 --> 00:45:42,954
Gang Ho will be mine!

749
00:45:42,954 --> 00:45:46,165
Today, I'll act out getting shot!

750
00:45:46,165 --> 00:45:48,399
In the middle of a war...

751
00:45:52,649 --> 00:45:54,922
Oh, Mother...

752
00:45:56,125 --> 00:45:58,701
Mother... I feel something hot on my belly...

753
00:46:00,065 --> 00:46:01,419
Oh, boy.

754
00:46:26,580 --> 00:46:28,485
Jung Woo Jae is here.

755
00:46:28,485 --> 00:46:30,470
Just go over there.

756
00:46:57,612 --> 00:46:59,821
Let's see him in action first.

757
00:46:59,821 --> 00:47:01,371
Yes, sir.

758
00:47:03,116 --> 00:47:06,912
Imagine that he's a threat to the female lead.

759
00:47:06,912 --> 00:47:09,312
- Let's see you take him down.
- Alright.

760
00:47:34,190 --> 00:47:35,703
What in the world?

761
00:47:44,955 --> 00:47:46,368
He's an absolute paragon!

762
00:47:46,368 --> 00:47:48,341
The cream of the crop!

763
00:47:49,181 --> 00:47:51,290
That's Gang Ho, for sure.

764
00:47:51,290 --> 00:47:53,334
Yoon Ha Na, and that guy...

765
00:47:53,334 --> 00:47:56,738
Their facial structures just
complement each other perfectly!

766
00:47:56,738 --> 00:48:00,610
I can see them lined up
for the ultimate optimal shot!

767
00:48:01,441 --> 00:48:03,551
Could you do that once more?

768
00:48:03,551 --> 00:48:04,834
Sure.

769
00:48:15,898 --> 00:48:18,084
Let's see how you look on camera.

770
00:48:20,277 --> 00:48:23,280
Imagine there's someone
whom you'd give your life to protect...

771
00:48:23,280 --> 00:48:26,787
standing in front of the camera,
and look into it.

772
00:48:28,536 --> 00:48:31,617
Ready, action!

773
00:49:12,204 --> 00:49:13,486
Cut.

774
00:49:19,253 --> 00:49:21,777
Have you ever acted before?

775
00:49:22,798 --> 00:49:25,175
No, not at all.

776
00:49:25,175 --> 00:49:27,919
That's fine. We can make do.

777
00:49:40,858 --> 00:49:43,861
I can't believe this!

778
00:49:43,861 --> 00:49:46,280
The national judo player, Lee Hyeong Won...

779
00:49:46,280 --> 00:49:48,824
he wants to take the audition!

780
00:49:48,824 --> 00:49:50,475
- Oh, my god!
- What? Lee Hyeong Won?

781
00:49:50,475 --> 00:49:52,511
Yeah, Lee Hyeong Won!

782
00:50:02,750 --> 00:50:04,771
Right this way.

783
00:50:15,953 --> 00:50:17,936
Hi, Yoon Ha Na.

784
00:50:17,936 --> 00:50:19,855
I heard you're the female lead.

785
00:50:19,855 --> 00:50:22,462
Yeah, I am.

786
00:50:26,779 --> 00:50:29,752
I'll play it. Your counterpart.

787
00:50:41,895 --> 00:50:45,339
Lee Hyeong Won
literally wants to act in our film.

788
00:50:45,339 --> 00:50:46,840
This is a great opportunity!

789
00:50:46,840 --> 00:50:48,776
What are we even on the fence about?

790
00:50:48,776 --> 00:50:52,938
We're guaranteed to go viral
if it gets on social media!

791
00:50:53,545 --> 00:50:55,516
What do you think, Ha Na?

792
00:50:55,516 --> 00:50:57,518
It's your counterpart, after all.

793
00:50:57,518 --> 00:51:01,379
I still think that Jung Woo Jae
explained the character,

794
00:51:01,379 --> 00:51:04,523
and his acting was way better
than Lee Hyeong Won.

795
00:51:05,318 --> 00:51:07,486
The director will do the explaining,

796
00:51:07,486 --> 00:51:09,363
and we can teach him to act.

797
00:51:09,363 --> 00:51:13,617
But you need to be born with that star quality.

798
00:51:13,617 --> 00:51:15,619
Wouldn't you agree, Director Yang?

799
00:51:15,619 --> 00:51:19,123
But still, we shouldn't decide
based on what would go viral.

800
00:51:19,123 --> 00:51:22,626
I think Jung Woo Jae's acting was superb.

801
00:51:22,626 --> 00:51:26,505
I honestly couldn't believe he's an amateur.
Gave me goosebumps.

802
00:51:26,505 --> 00:51:28,716
Don't you think so, Jun Mo?

803
00:51:28,716 --> 00:51:31,802
I think that... Mr. Jung Woo Jae?

804
00:51:31,802 --> 00:51:36,677
His actions and acting
had that deeply touching element to it.

805
00:51:36,677 --> 00:51:38,016
"Mr. Jung Woo Jae?" Really?

806
00:51:38,016 --> 00:51:39,435
You rat.

807
00:51:39,435 --> 00:51:41,645
This is what's wrong with our society,
everything's based on connections.

808
00:51:41,645 --> 00:51:43,671
I know you were in the same judo team
as him in high school.

809
00:51:43,671 --> 00:51:44,845
Is that why you're siding with him?

810
00:51:44,845 --> 00:51:46,316
- No.
- "No?"

811
00:51:46,316 --> 00:51:49,080
You think you're cheeky, huh?
Yeah, you've got some cheek right here.

812
00:51:49,080 --> 00:51:52,197
Going viral is what makes a film successful.

813
00:51:52,197 --> 00:51:56,660
With Lee Hyeong Won's name value added,
this film will go places, I assure you!

814
00:51:56,660 --> 00:52:00,331
Well, optically speaking...

815
00:52:00,331 --> 00:52:03,625
Yoon Ha Na and Jung Woo Jae
would make the most visually satisfying pair.

816
00:52:03,625 --> 00:52:06,203
So, you prefer Jung Woo Jae?

817
00:52:06,203 --> 00:52:08,714
Yeah, but even if we decided on Lee Hyeong Won,

818
00:52:08,714 --> 00:52:12,676
I could work my magic
with the '62 vintage Zeiss...

819
00:52:12,676 --> 00:52:15,236
There's no need to worry.

820
00:52:23,687 --> 00:52:25,436
I've made up my mind.

821
00:52:28,998 --> 00:52:31,270
- Lee Hyeong Won.
- Yes!

822
00:52:33,614 --> 00:52:35,511
And Jung Woo Jae.

823
00:52:39,787 --> 00:52:41,685
The two will have another audition.

824
00:52:49,296 --> 00:52:52,439
That Lee Hyeong Won, or whatever,
took Woo Jae's place in the national team,

825
00:52:52,439 --> 00:52:55,069
and he wants to meddle with his life again?

826
00:52:57,809 --> 00:52:58,917
Jung Woo Jae.

827
00:52:58,917 --> 00:53:01,994
I'll train you myself,
the best actress of the year.

828
00:53:05,185 --> 00:53:06,788
[That Summer, Us]

829
00:53:09,739 --> 00:53:10,943
<i>I'll play it.</i>

830
00:53:10,943 --> 00:53:12,420
<i>Your counterpart.</i>

831
00:53:15,320 --> 00:53:17,981
A callback audition, huh?

832
00:53:23,365 --> 00:53:25,636
[Gang Ho approaches So Hee and
holds her hand tight, as if he'd never let go]

833
00:53:26,874 --> 00:53:29,419
Holding hands is just holding hands.

834
00:53:29,419 --> 00:53:31,605
What's with all these "tightly" shenanigans?

835
00:53:35,772 --> 00:53:37,801
[Gang Ho embraces So Hee and pats her back.
The two are pressed up against each other]

836
00:53:37,801 --> 00:53:41,930
"Press up against each other?" What? Why?

837
00:53:41,930 --> 00:53:43,640
What's wrong with this director guy anyway?

838
00:53:43,640 --> 00:53:45,331
Yang Jun Mo? You...

839
00:53:49,438 --> 00:53:52,002
[A long, deep, intimate kiss
to confirm their love]

840
00:53:55,522 --> 00:53:57,239
"K-kiss?"

841
00:53:57,239 --> 00:53:58,906
"A long kiss?"

842
00:53:58,906 --> 00:54:01,076
How long?

843
00:54:01,076 --> 00:54:02,528
Oh, no.

844
00:54:04,539 --> 00:54:08,750
That means Ha Na might have to shoot this
with that bastard, Lee Hyeong Won...

845
00:54:08,750 --> 00:54:09,870
A deep kiss?

846
00:54:09,870 --> 00:54:11,378
Not a peck, a real kiss...

847
00:54:11,378 --> 00:54:13,488
A kiss...

848
00:54:13,488 --> 00:54:15,257
Not smooching, a kiss...

849
00:54:15,257 --> 00:54:16,994
Should I just beg her not to do it?

850
00:54:17,718 --> 00:54:20,067
Woo Jae, are you busy?

851
00:54:21,383 --> 00:54:22,831
Just a moment.

852
00:54:26,476 --> 00:54:27,860
<i>Tightly held hands?</i>

853
00:54:27,860 --> 00:54:30,559
<i>Pressing up against each other? A long kiss?</i>

854
00:54:35,360 --> 00:54:37,243
Let's do this.

855
00:54:37,243 --> 00:54:38,512
Okay...

856
00:54:47,252 --> 00:54:48,916
[Scene 1. A lone bus stop, daytime]

857
00:54:48,916 --> 00:54:51,738
[Gang Ho says his last goodbye to So Hee]

858
00:54:51,738 --> 00:54:53,419
I wish you the best.

859
00:54:53,419 --> 00:54:55,587
[So Hee, however...]
I'll be going now.

860
00:54:55,587 --> 00:54:57,196
[grabs Gang Ho's hand.]

861
00:54:59,508 --> 00:55:01,273
Don't go.

862
00:55:18,865 --> 00:55:21,097
[Scene 4. The bus stop, daytime]

863
00:55:21,097 --> 00:55:26,501
[So Hee cries tears of relief
in Gang Ho's arms]

864
00:55:26,501 --> 00:55:29,275
[Gang Ho embraces her and pats her shoulder]

865
00:55:31,083 --> 00:55:33,115
You need to pat my back.

866
00:55:52,312 --> 00:55:54,462
[Scene 6. Road leading out of town, daytime]

867
00:55:54,462 --> 00:55:56,620
[The two look at each other]

868
00:55:56,620 --> 00:56:00,529
[Gang Ho hugs So Hee, and whispers in her ear]

869
00:56:00,529 --> 00:56:02,146
I promise.

870
00:56:02,823 --> 00:56:06,670
I'll never leave you all alone.

871
00:56:34,144 --> 00:56:37,252
Ha Na, you're great at acting.

872
00:56:37,252 --> 00:56:38,725
Yeah...

873
00:56:38,725 --> 00:56:41,319
Got a grasp on what emotions
you should be conveying?

874
00:56:41,319 --> 00:56:43,972
Yeah, I get it too well.

875
00:56:48,408 --> 00:56:50,943
I was actually wondering...

876
00:56:51,847 --> 00:56:56,023
Do you do everything that the script says?

877
00:56:57,497 --> 00:56:59,294
Yeah, that's how it works.

878
00:57:00,380 --> 00:57:01,849
Is that so?

879
00:57:05,427 --> 00:57:07,929
Well, most of the time,
we follow the script as is.

880
00:57:07,929 --> 00:57:11,308
But sometimes, we add in more spice on the set.

881
00:57:11,308 --> 00:57:13,060
What?

882
00:57:13,060 --> 00:57:16,746
Or sometimes, we water it down, too.

883
00:57:16,746 --> 00:57:18,477
Oh, okay.

884
00:57:21,149 --> 00:57:22,778
Are you angry?

885
00:57:22,778 --> 00:57:24,279
Angry?

886
00:57:24,279 --> 00:57:27,565
What? No, I'm not.

887
00:57:35,207 --> 00:57:36,999
Lee Hyeong Won...

888
00:57:37,584 --> 00:57:39,623
must be practicing, too, right?

889
00:57:42,964 --> 00:57:44,631
Why?

890
00:57:44,631 --> 00:57:46,422
Does it bother you?

891
00:57:47,969 --> 00:57:51,803
Let's be honest. He's at an advantage.

892
00:57:51,803 --> 00:57:54,009
He's famous, you know.

893
00:57:54,810 --> 00:57:56,562
Jung Woo Jae.

894
00:57:57,646 --> 00:57:59,344
Don't be scared.

895
00:58:01,566 --> 00:58:05,091
The way I see it, you should play Gang Ho.

896
00:58:05,091 --> 00:58:06,988
You're Gang Ho himself.

897
00:58:06,988 --> 00:58:10,272
So, believe in yourself.

898
00:58:13,551 --> 00:58:14,948
Me?

899
00:58:17,100 --> 00:58:21,381
But he and I are both amateurs anyway.

900
00:58:21,381 --> 00:58:25,045
If we're similar in skill,
of course they'd pick the celebrity.

901
00:58:25,045 --> 00:58:28,009
Similar? No, he's not even close!

902
00:58:28,009 --> 00:58:32,300
Besides, you have something that he doesn't.

903
00:58:32,300 --> 00:58:34,057
What?

904
00:58:34,057 --> 00:58:37,766
Jung Woo Jae's very own personal coach,
Yoon Ha Na!

905
00:58:40,040 --> 00:58:43,191
Yeah, you're right.

906
00:58:43,191 --> 00:58:44,943
If you can't put faith in yourself,

907
00:58:44,943 --> 00:58:47,582
put faith in me, who believes in you.

908
00:58:48,396 --> 00:58:49,803
Got it?

909
00:58:50,615 --> 00:58:51,964
Okay.

910
00:59:06,454 --> 00:59:08,326
In the script,

911
00:59:08,963 --> 00:59:11,741
everyone calls So Hee "misfortune."

912
00:59:11,741 --> 00:59:16,808
Everyone around her ends up miserable.

913
00:59:16,808 --> 00:59:19,895
But letting that fear
of the future get a hold of you,

914
00:59:19,895 --> 00:59:22,722
and leaving someone you love because of it?

915
00:59:22,722 --> 00:59:26,526
I think that's what's most unfortunate.

916
00:59:26,526 --> 00:59:30,322
So I do understand Gang Ho, to a degree.

917
00:59:30,322 --> 00:59:33,517
I think we have a lot in common.

918
00:59:35,243 --> 00:59:39,071
What do you think he'd be like?

919
00:59:42,355 --> 00:59:45,594
I think he's someone
who always keeps a promise.

920
00:59:46,240 --> 00:59:50,186
Even when the whole world
changes and turns its back,

921
00:59:50,186 --> 00:59:53,611
he'd remember his promise
to So Hee and stay by her side.

922
00:59:53,611 --> 00:59:55,374
That's who he is.

923
00:59:56,141 --> 00:59:57,696
A promise...

924
01:00:00,310 --> 01:00:02,187
<i>I'll confess to you again, properly...</i>

925
01:00:02,187 --> 01:00:04,314
<i>after the trials.</i>

926
01:00:04,314 --> 01:00:05,857
<i>When I make the national team,</i>

927
01:00:05,857 --> 01:00:07,943
<i>and you get admitted to your dream college...</i>

928
01:00:07,943 --> 01:00:10,093
<i>we'll talk again.</i>

929
01:00:14,783 --> 01:00:17,118
Hey, Ha Na.

930
01:00:17,118 --> 01:00:18,662
Yeah?

931
01:00:18,662 --> 01:00:19,963
I...

932
01:00:21,665 --> 01:00:23,667
I have something I need to tell you.

933
01:00:23,667 --> 01:00:26,544
I wanted to say it sooner...

934
01:00:26,544 --> 01:00:27,794
But...

935
01:00:27,794 --> 01:00:30,465
I injured myself after I made the team,

936
01:00:30,465 --> 01:00:32,842
and then got busy applying for college...

937
01:00:32,842 --> 01:00:35,220
and you got into your dream college.

938
01:00:35,220 --> 01:00:36,596
And...

939
01:00:36,596 --> 01:00:38,765
I... I mean...

940
01:00:38,765 --> 01:00:40,225
<i>When I make the national team,</i>

941
01:00:40,225 --> 01:00:41,834
<i>and you get admitted to your dream college...</i>

942
01:00:41,834 --> 01:00:44,101
<i>we'll talk again.</i>

943
01:00:53,153 --> 01:00:54,728
I...

944
01:00:56,741 --> 01:00:58,669
really like you.

945
01:01:01,621 --> 01:01:04,782
I really mean it.

946
01:01:06,876 --> 01:01:09,253
I like you a lot.

947
01:01:09,253 --> 01:01:10,743
Ha Na.

948
01:02:21,326 --> 01:02:22,843
What's going on here?

949
01:03:09,041 --> 01:03:11,974
<i>He keeps trying to take over Woo Jae's place.</i>

950
01:03:12,594 --> 01:03:14,768
<i>Why is he so tangled up in our business?</i>

951
01:03:14,768 --> 01:03:15,792
<i>No way.</i>

952
01:03:15,792 --> 01:03:17,822
<i>I. Yoon Ha Na, 34 years old...</i>

953
01:03:17,822 --> 01:03:19,746
<i>Ha Na!</i>

954
01:03:19,746 --> 01:03:22,041
<i>- He's so confident!
- Give me your number!</i>

955
01:03:22,041 --> 01:03:24,245
<i>Is your heart beating yet?</i>

956
01:03:25,305 --> 01:03:28,599
<i>I don't care what you do to me. But...</i>

957
01:03:28,599 --> 01:03:30,706
<i>I won't let you hurt Ha Na.</i>

958
01:03:32,068 --> 01:03:34,694
<i>Hey. What's this?</i>

959
01:03:34,694 --> 01:03:36,718
<i>There's no need to be afraid.</i>

960
01:03:36,718 --> 01:03:38,442
<i>I'll protect you, no matter what.</i>

961
01:03:38,442 --> 01:03:39,779
<i>No!</i>
